---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro'
---

<Layout 
  title="Dark Matter Substructure Cheat Sheet | Free Subhalos, Stream, Tidal Tails"
  description="Complete dark matter substructure cheat sheet with subhalos, streams, and tidal tails. Free download for physics students."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <h1>Dark Matter Substructure<br><span>Cheat Sheet</span></h1>
    <p>Subhalos, streams, and tidal tails. From dwarf galaxies to dark matter clumps.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Subhalos</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Properties</h3>
        <pre><code>Small dark matter halos within larger halos
Hierarchical structure formation
Milky Way: ~ 50-100 subhalos > 10⁷ M_sun
Satellite galaxies: luminous subhalos
Dark subhalos: no stars</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Tidal Streams</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Formation</h3>
        <pre><code>Tidal disruption of satellite galaxies
Stars stripped into streams
Preserve orbital information
Example: Sagittarius stream
Probes dark matter halo shape</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Missing Satellites Problem</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Problem</h3>
        <pre><code>CDM predicts ~ 500 subhalos > 10⁷ M_sun
Observation: ~ 50 satellite galaxies
Discrepancy: factor of 10
Solutions: reionization, baryonic feedback, warm DM</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Dwarf Galaxies</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Types</h3>
        <pre><code>Dwarf spheroidal (dSph): low luminosity, high M/L
Dwarf irregular (dIrr): gas-rich, star-forming
Ultra-faint dwarfs: barely detectable
Highest M/L ratios: most DM-dominated</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Download</h2>
    <p>Print this page or save as PDF for quick reference.</p>
    <p><strong>Tip:</strong> Use Ctrl+P (Cmd+P on Mac) to print or save as PDF.</p>
  </section>
</Layout>
